# overlay/profiles/desktop/packages.list — the DPorts packages of the
# desktop profile.
#
# Copyright (c) 2026 The wtfbsd contributors. BSD-2-Clause (see LICENSE).
#
# One DPorts ORIGIN per line (category/port); blank lines and
# #-comments are ignored. The build hands the packages to the release
# tooling of DragonFly, which puts them into the release root:
#
#   DPORTS_EXTRA_PACKAGES="<the packages of the base list and of the
#                            profile list>"
#
# The names are DPorts origins and not bare package names: dsynth takes
# origins only (category/port), and a bare name is only understood under
# the binpkgs modifier of the release tooling, which this template does
# not use. The release tooling builds them from the DPorts tree, whose
# path is DPORTS_PATH (/usr/dports by default).
#
# The desktop is X11 with Xfce and the LightDM greeter; there is no
# Wayland anywhere in this distribution.
#
# The origins below were checked against the DPorts tree of DragonFly
# (the directory of every one of them exists):
#
# x11/xorg: the X11 server of DragonFly.
# x11/lightdm: the display manager.
# x11/lightdm-gtk-greeter: the greeter of LightDM (there is no
# x11/lightdm-gtk2-greeter in DPorts).
# x11-wm/xfce4: the metaport of the Xfce desktop: it brings the window
# manager, the session, the panel and the terminal.
# x11-fm/thunar: the file manager of the desktop.
#
# The modifier "gui" of the release tooling of DragonFly (make gui
# release) installs a set of its own; the names below are the ones of
# this overlay, so that the desktop does not depend on what that
# modifier happens to bring.
#
x11/xorg
x11/lightdm
x11/lightdm-gtk-greeter
x11-wm/xfce4
x11-fm/thunar
